    "description": "Ask one incident's five questions (parameter incident, its name) and answer each in three states: found (posted), none (run summary only) or unknown (posted as a gap naming the pull or statement that would answer it). RQ1 which deployments run an affected release; RQ2 is each exposure patched (missing, overdue, disputed; none only when a full scan verified it; excepted while an approved exception for each of its CVEs has not expired, then missing again); RQ3 were we exploited in the window, per service (none only for not_exploited with complete reads of every stated log source covering the window); RQ4 which credentials warrant rotation (posted with the audit and patch state; rotating after a verified patch is the recommended order, the agent's call), and is each rotation verified by a separate state read; RQ5 can the incident close (ready_to_close, with any unknown audit as accepted residue). A closed incident posts nothing. Observe-only. Runs as a Line (parameters incident, inventory_pull, log_pull, credential_pull, record_pull): daily, on a landing, after a window closes, or line run.",
